{"name":"Let It Snow","hex":"#d8f1f4","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"let it snow","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Phrase","definitions":["Used around the Christmas season to express anticipation of snowfall."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/let_it_snow"}],"entries":[{"title":"Let It Snow (2019 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Let it Snow is a 2019 American Christmas romantic comedy film directed by Luke Snellin from a screenplay by Kay Cannon, Victoria Strouse and Laura Solon, based on the young adult novel of the same name by Maureen Johnson, John Green, and Lauren Myracle."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/b5/Let_It_Snow_poster.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Let_It_Snow_(2019_film)","wikidata":"Q22046828"},{"title":"Let It Snow (2020 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Let It Snow is a 2020 horror thriller film co-written and directed by Stanislav Kapralov. It stars Ivanna Sakhno, Alex Hafner and Tinatin Dalakishvili."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/8c/Let_It_Snow_2020_Poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Let_It_Snow_(2020_film)","wikidata":"Q104412858"},{"title":"Let It Snow! Let It Snow! Let It Snow!","blocks":[{"text":"\"Let It Snow! Let It Snow! Let It Snow!\", also known as simply \"Let It Snow\", is a song written by lyricist Sammy Cahn and composer Jule Styne in July 1945 in Hollywood, California, during a heatwave as Cahn and Styne imagined cooler conditions. The song was first recorded that fall by Vaughn Monroe, was released just after Thanksgiving, and became a hit by Christmas."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Let_It_Snow!_Let_It_Snow!_Let_It_Snow!","wikidata":"Q1089150"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/b/b5/Let_It_Snow_poster.jpeg/250px-Let_It_Snow_poster.jpeg?utm_sourc